   "source": [
    "<font size=6> <b> Week 8 Lecture Notebook: Introduction to Large Language Models (LLMs) </b> </font>\\n",
    "<div class=\\"alert alert-block alert-success\\">\\n",
    " In this session, we will explore the world of Large Language Models (LLMs) and learn how to use the Hugging Face Transformers library to perform common NLP tasks.<br>\\n",
    "</div>\\n",
    "<p style=\\"text-align:right;\\"> sumyeon@gmail.com </p>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Introduction to Hugging Face Transformers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The Hugging Face `transformers` library is a powerful tool that provides a unified interface to thousands of pre-trained models for a wide range of NLP tasks. It simplifies the process of downloading, loading, and using state-of-the-art models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "First, let's install the `transformers` library:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install transformers[torch]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Using Pipelines for Common NLP Tasks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Pipelines are the easiest way to get started with the `transformers` library. They provide a simple API for performing a variety of tasks with pre-trained models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sentiment Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import pipeline\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Using a specific model for sentiment analysis\\n",
    "sentiment_analyzer = pipeline('sentiment-analysis', model='distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english')\\n",
    "result = sentiment_analyzer('I love the new design of the website!')\\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Text Generation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using a specific model for text generation\\n",
    "text_generator = pipeline('text-generation', model='gpt2')\\n",
    "result = text_generator('In a world where AI is becoming more prevalent,', max_length=50, num_return_sequences=1)\\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Question Answering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using a specific model for question answering\\n",
    "question_answerer = pipeline('question-answering', model='distilbert-base-cased-distilled-squad')\\n",
    "context = 'The Hugging Face Transformers library provides a unified interface to thousands of pre-trained models.'\\n",
    "question = 'What does the Hugging Face Transformers library provide?'\\n",
    "result = question_answerer(question=question, context=context)\\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Zero-Shot Classification"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using a specific model for zero-shot classification\\n",
    "classifier = pipeline('zero-shot-classification', model='facebook/bart-large-mnli')\\n",
    "result = classifier(\\n",
    "    'This is a course about the Transformers library.',\\n",
    "    candidate_labels=['education', 'politics', 'business'],\\n",
    ")\\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Named Entity Recognition (NER)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using a specific model for NER\\n",
    "ner_pipeline = pipeline('ner', model='dbmdz/bert-large-cased-finetuned-conll03-english')\\n",
    "result = ner_pipeline('My name is Jules and I live in Seoul.')\\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Working with Models and Tokenizers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "While pipelines are great for quick and easy use, you can also work directly with models and tokenizers for more control. This is what you'll typically do when you need to fine-tune a model on your own data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Tokenization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Tokenization is the process of converting raw text into a format that the model can understand. This usually involves splitting the text into words or subwords (tokens) and then converting those tokens into numerical IDs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer\\n",
    "\\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('bert-base-uncased')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Tokenize a single sentence\\n",
    "inputs = tokenizer('Hello, world!', return_tensors='pt')\\n",
    "print('Tokens:', tokenizer.convert_ids_to_tokens(inputs['input_ids'][0]))\\n",
    "print('Input IDs:', inputs['input_ids'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Model Inference"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Once the text is tokenized, you can pass it to the model to get predictions. The model returns logits, which are the raw, unnormalized scores for each class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification\\n",
    "import torch\\n",
    "\\n",
    "model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained('bert-base-uncased')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\\n",
    "    logits = model(**inputs).logits\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print('Logits:', logits)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpreting the Output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To get the final prediction, you can apply a softmax function to the logits to get probabilities, and then take the argmax to get the class with the highest probability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "predicted_class_id = torch.argmax(logits, dim=1).item()\\n",
    "print(f'Predicted class ID: {predicted_class_id}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This notebook provides a brief introduction to the Hugging Face Transformers library. There are many more models and tasks to explore, so be sure to check out the official documentation for more information."
   ]
  }
 ],
